  "_comment": "Settings for the headless jira-to-pr agent (run with cwd agents/jira-to-pr). Edits allowed only in workspace/ and the two real checkouts (absolute, symlink-resolved paths of products/*/codebase/*). curl is limited to the Jira REST API; local HTTP checks run via docker exec inside the stack containers (config/environments/local.md). node is limited to the lockcheck CLI. Bash(scripts/*) was removed: the agent must not run run-agent.sh (would spawn a nested run) or clone-repos.sh (no cloning in this mode). The deny list is a speed bump against mistakes, not a sandbox: the rules in CLAUDE.md, the subagent prompts and the target environment file remain binding. Wrapping a forbidden command in docker exec (e.g. docker exec ... sh -c '<forbidden>') is still forbidden. Known MVP gap: prompt injection via ticket text is not mitigated (trusted ticket authors, single laptop)."
